---
/**
 * About block, from Figma 1:15789.
 *
 * The reference heads this section with a handwritten "Good
 * morning". It is the one warm note in an otherwise instrument-like
 * page, and it works because it is time-aware: it greets you
 * according to YOUR clock, so it reads as addressed rather than
 * decorative.
 *
 * Server-rendered from the site's own timezone first, then
 * corrected client-side to the visitor's. Without the correction a
 * visitor in London gets "Good evening" at breakfast, which is
 * worse than no greeting at all.
 */
import { site } from "../../config/site";

const hour = Number(
  new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
    timeZone: site.timezone,
    hour: "2-digit",
    hour12: false,
  }).format(new Date())
);
const initial =
  hour < 5 ? "Still up?" : hour < 12 ? "Good morning" : hour < 18 ? "Good afternoon" : "Good evening";
---

<div>
  <p
    class="text-title font-medium text-ink" data-greeting
  >
    {initial}
  </p>

  <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
    <li class="bullet prose-measure">
      I am <strong class="font-medium text-ink">{site.name}</strong>, an AI
      engineer in {site.location}, reading two degrees at once:{" "}
      <span class="text-ink">Computer Science</span> at Example Institute of
      Technology and <span class="text-ink">Data Science and AI</span> at
      Example University.
    </li>
    <li class="bullet prose-measure">
      The combination is the point. Most of my machine learning ends up attached
      to a sensor, a machine, or a process that will keep running whether or not
      the model is right, which is a different discipline from getting a good
      number in a notebook.
    </li>
    <li class="bullet prose-measure">
      What I actually care about is measurement. Every project on this site
      states its baseline, its evaluation set, and the conditions under which it
      fails. A metric without those three is a decoration.
    </li>
    <li class="bullet prose-measure">
      Currently: bearing-fault detection on live CNC spindles at the{" "}
      <span class="text-ink">Smart Manufacturing Lab</span>, and looking for an
      AI/ML internship for summer 2027.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<style>
  /* Bullets are drawn rather than list-style, so the dot can be a
     token colour and sit on the first line's optical centre. */
  .bullet {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.125rem;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16px;
  }
  .bullet::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.125rem;
    top: 0.625rem;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 999px
    ;
    background-color: var(--color-ink-4);
  }
</style>

<script>
  /* Correct the greeting to the VISITOR's clock. The server can
     only know Ashutosh's timezone, and this line is addressed to
     whoever is reading it. */
  const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-greeting]");
  if (el) {
    const h = new Date().getHours();
    el.textContent =
      h < 5
        ? "Still up?"
        : h < 12
          ? "Good morning"
          : h < 18
            ? "Good afternoon"
            : "Good evening";
  }
</script>
